  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Starting from the foot of the Notre-Dame-des-Maures track, wide forest tracks lead to the Gaoutabry dolmen, the largest dolmen in the Var: a Neolithic collective tomb listed on the Historic Monuments inventory. Allow 2.3 km (150 m of elevation gain) to reach it according to the tourist office, which also offers a 7.2 km "Le Gaoutabry" circuit with views of the sea, the Salins d'Hyères and the Îles d'Or.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The tourist office publishes no dog rule for this route; keep your dog on a leash. The key point: access is regulated by the fire alarm plan from 21 June to 20 September. From June to September, check the fire risk map (updated at 5pm for the next day) or call the tourist office (04 94 01 53 10) before setting off. The car park at the foot of the track is free.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: always check access to the massif in summer before hitting the road.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>La Londe-les-Maures and its vineyards are close by, a good excuse to extend the outing.</p>
